	(no_connect
		(at 241.3 612.14)
		(uuid "b27a646a-18c9-5cf9-a782-675b52101fdc")
	)
	(text_box "Function: the DISC_OUT finger of U01_BCD1 is left open (no-connect flag). Nothing on this board or on the FPGA side reads it.\nSource / changes: inherited from the ASIC designer's board pair, changed in V6. Reference: meeting with the ASIC designer, 12 Nov 2026, notes V1, answer A3 (DISC_OUT is not needed: \"It does not even need to be connected to the chip.\"), file 2026-11-12_FPGA_Work/07_Meeting_With_ASIC_Designer_V1/MEETING_NOTES_V1.md (a project record, no web address). Changed against V5: label T_DISC_OUT and its 8.89 mm stub wire removed, no-connect flag added on the pin; no part added or removed. Connector pins 3 and 5 keep the names DISC_OUT(2) and DISC_OUT and still pass J3 to J4. Not verified: this rests on the designer's spoken answer; no chip data sheet page states that the pad may float. V8 (Howard, 16 Nov 2026; pin map V7, review R2S-05): connector pins 3 and 5 of J3 and J4, which carried the DISC_OUT labels, are now DGND, adding two ground contacts per connector."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 250 366 0)
		(size 112 29.0)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0.2)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "6a510d58-ef31-5560-bfbb-b401dbfd8a9b")
	)
	(text_box "Function: the DISC_OUT finger of U01_BCD2 is left open (no-connect flag). Nothing on this board or on the FPGA side reads it.\nSource / changes: inherited from the ASIC designer's board pair, changed in V6. Reference: meeting with the ASIC designer, 12 Nov 2026, notes V1, answer A3 (DISC_OUT is not needed: \"It does not even need to be connected to the chip.\"), file 2026-11-12_FPGA_Work/07_Meeting_With_ASIC_Designer_V1/MEETING_NOTES_V1.md (a project record, no web address). Changed against V5: label T_DISC_OUT(2) and its 8.89 mm stub wire removed, no-connect flag added on the pin; no part added or removed. Connector pins 3 and 5 keep the names DISC_OUT(2) and DISC_OUT and still pass J3 to J4. Not verified: this rests on the designer's spoken answer; no chip data sheet page states that the pad may float. V8 (Howard, 16 Nov 2026; pin map V7, review R2S-05): connector pins 3 and 5 of J3 and J4, which carried the DISC_OUT labels, are now DGND, adding two ground contacts per connector."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 250 619 0)
		(size 112 29.0)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0.2)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "1f492b0d-5f39-5431-8e61-583834d185ba")
	)
	(text_box "Function: J1 is a single AGND pin position. From V6 it is not fitted (do not populate, not in the BOM, not in the position file); the plated hole and its AGND connection stay on the board.\nSource / changes: inherited from the ASIC designer's board pair, changed in V6. Reference: meeting with the ASIC designer, 12 Nov 2026, notes V1, answer E6 (J1: \"Not needed.\"), file 2026-11-12_FPGA_Work/07_Meeting_With_ASIC_Designer_V1/MEETING_NOTES_V1.md (a project record, no web address). Changed against V5: only the three part flags; footprint, position, hole and net are as in V5."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 425 66 0)
		(size 112 16)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
