	(text_box "Function: local decoupling for the ASIC supply rails. Each 1.5 V rail has two capacitors per chip on B.Cu under the dies (10 nF nearest the die, 100 nF in the outer row). VDD_CGEN, VDD10 (+8 V) and VSS10 (-8 V) have their pairs on F.Cu at the connector, and C63 adds a VDD_CGEN capacitor beside chip 1. They supply the chips' fast switching current and keep it off the rails, whose regulators sit on the LDO board behind J3/J4.\nSource / changes: positions and nets inherited from the ASIC designer's board pair (no data sheet circuit). Values from the ASIC designer in a short talk on 17 Nov 2026 (\"you can use a 10 nano or 100\", for every rail), recorded in 2026-11-17_FPGA_Work/11_Gerald_Quick_Talk_ASIC_Caps_V1/START_HERE.md (a project record, no web address; machine transcript). Changed in V9 against V8: values set (10 nF: C1, C2, C4, C5, C6, C7, C14, C18, C25, C33, C34, C41, C42, C46, C48; 100 nF: C19, C26, C50-C63); parts Murata GRM033R71E103KE14D, LCSC C85930, X7R 25 V 0201 (https://www.murata.com/en-us/products/productdetail?partno=GRM033R71E103KE14%23) and Samsung CL03A104KA3NNNC, LCSC C307379, X5R 25 V 0201 (https://product.samsungsem.com/mlcc/CL03A104KA3NNN.do); C63 (VDD_CGEN, 100 nF) added, placed beside chip 1 in V9; symbols redrawn by Claude onto local rail and ground buses with the same nets. Not verified: no chip data sheet states the decoupling requirement; C63 at 100 nF is Howard's choice (17 Nov) over the 1 uF (\"1000\") also mentioned; 100 nF X5R at 8 V keeps only part of its value (DC bias)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 190.5 106.68 0)
		(size 203.2 25.4)
