			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "aab878bc-0336-4590-a35b-0b6d00d6fe17")
	)
	(text_box "Function: J3 (receptacle, underside) and J4 (plug, top side) are the 80-contact stacking connectors of the head. Each J3 contact goes to the same-numbered J4 contact, so all 80 lines pass through this board to the next one. Pins 3 and 5 are DGND (pin map V7).\nSource / changes: pin order inherited from the ASIC designer and final (meeting 12 Nov 2026, answer A1, record 2026-11-12_FPGA_Work/07_Meeting_With_ASIC_Designer_V1/MEETING_NOTES_V1.md, a project record, no web address); not a data sheet circuit. V6 took both chips' DISC_OUT fingers off pins 3 and 5 (answer A3); V8 made both pins DGND (Howard, 16 Nov 2026). V15, part fields only, no net or copper change: J3 = Hirose DF40C-80DS-0.4V(51) (HRS No. CL0684-4002-0-51, LCSC C312960), J4 = Hirose DF40C-80DP-0.4V(51) (HRS No. CL0684-4001-8-51, LCSC C294544), the same pair as J3/J4 of the FPGA-LDO A board they mate with; stacking (mated) height 1.5 mm. Reference: Hirose DF40 Series Catalog, Jan. 2025, p. 6 (product number structure: no height code = 1.5 mm), p. 8 (receptacle table, stacking height 1.5 mm) and p. 14 (plug table), https://www.hirose.com/en/product/series/DF40/documents?path=%2Fapi%2Fv1%2Fseries%2FDF40%2Fdocuments%2Fproduct_series_catalog%2Fcontent%3Flang%3DEN Not verified: the catalog states this connector has no polarity (p. 8 note 4, p. 14 note 5), so a pair can be mated turned 180 degrees and only the silkscreen marks guard against it; mated height and clearance over the dies and bond wires are not measured on hardware."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 400 462 0)
		(size 180 25)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
